<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan money market rates seesaw to end down.</title>
<headline>Pakistan money market rates seesaw to end down.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's money market rates fluctuated widely on Friday before ending lower amid excess liquidity, dealers said.</p>
<p>Early overnight offers were seen in the range of 18 and 17 percent, a dealer at Standard Chartered Bank said.</p>
<p>At midday, most of the deals were done in the range of 17 and 15 percent but excess liquidity forced lenders to lower offers and the market closed at 10 percent, he said.</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
